    A15_SMSS_71_M016935_026                                                   
                                                                              
    Apollo 15 Soil Mechanics                                                  
    Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) Page D-5                         
                                                                              
    Post-Flight Load Calibration - Data and Analysis                          
                                                                              
    These handwritten tables give the information used to perform the load    
    calibration on the Apollo 15 Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP).    
    The upper table gives the reading for each index corresponding to the     
    initial setting on the LSRP for a given load and the average value for    
    each load in degrees-minutes, decimal degrees, and millimeters.  The      
    lower table gives the load calibration factor in Newtons/millimeter for   
    each load level.  The chart is dated 13 August 1971, at U.C Berkeley.     
                                                                              
